# C091: Failed PyMem_Resize destroys the pending-call queue pointer
#
# CONFIRMED — static analysis (NULL dereference / resource leak)
#
# PyMem_Resize is an assigning macro (util.c:154-176).  On failure it overwrites
# the global pending_call_slots with NULL while count remains nonzero, leaks the
# old allocation, and leaves the already-registered dispatcher to index NULL.
# It also fails to establish MemoryError.  Requires memory exhaustion to trigger.
